Confocal microscopy images demonstrate that Nano-11 significantly enhances antigen uptake by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). While soluble FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA) alone shows minimal internalization by BMDCs, the cells efficiently phagocytize AF647-labeled Nano-11 particles. Crucially, when OVA is adsorbed onto Nano-11, both components are taken up in large quantities and co-localize within the BMDCs, indicating that Nano-11 serves as an effective delivery vehicle for antigens. This enhanced delivery is vital for promoting dendritic cell activation and subsequent immune responses.